Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.80,0:00:03.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}What if a volcano erupted in the middle of your city?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.30,0:00:05.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It starts with small earthquakes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.30,0:00:06.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Cracks in the street.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.50,0:00:09.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Steam rises from the asphalt.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.00,0:00:09.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.80,0:00:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Lava bursts out at over one thousand degrees.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.80,0:00:15.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}An ash cloud rises kilometers into the sky.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.60,0:00:17.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Day turns into night.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.00,0:00:18.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}That ash isn't smoke.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:21.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}It's tiny shards of rock and glass.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.20,0:00:28.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And the deadliest part… a cloud of hot gas and ash races down the streets at up to seven hundred kilometers per hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.60,0:00:29.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}But here's the twist.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.80,0:00:32.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Most lava moves slowly enough to walk away from.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.80,0:00:34.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}And it has happened before.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.30,0:00:42.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}In 1943, a volcano was born in a Mexican cornfield… and grew fifty meters in one day.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.00,0:00:43.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}So remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.00,0:00:47.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Auckland, New Zealand, is built on top of about fifty volcanoes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.50,0:00:49.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(150,150)}Would you live there?
